  "tag_consumption": {
    "reader_gate": "the exit reader branches on the entry count word alone (temp+0x60, loaded 0x4749b1d, tested 0x4749b25): zero copies temp[0..0x50] to the out union, nonzero writes {6, cap, buffer, count} with the discriminant store at 0x4749b3a; no tag word is loaded",
    "consumer_gate": "the consumer compares the out union word at 0x15a5930 against 6 only; the non-6 arm copies 0x48 bytes to the [rsp+0x278] destination without loading any entry",
    "debug_format": "the Err value is formatted only through its vtable Debug pointer 0x15b4420 (size-24 value = the entry vector header), reached from the unwrap helper through the dyn dispatch shim 0x1687260; it has no direct call site in the binary",
    "drop": "the entry vector drop 0x15ac470 walks entries at stride 0x20; for each entry it compares the tag word at +0x00 against 3 (unsigned <=, 0x15ac4a9) and, when the +0x8 word is nonzero, frees (+0x10, +0x8) through the dealloc slot 0x64df4a0; the +0x18 word is never loaded and no tag value selects a different path; the buffer is freed at cap << 5",
    "per_tag_dispatch_found": false
  },
  "destination_chain": [
    "consumer rdi argument, saved at [rsp+0x278] in the prologue (0x15a3ba1) and loaded once, at the exit copy (0x15a5940)",
    "the wrapper 0x15a6510 passes its own frame scratch at [rsp+0x48] as that rdi (0x15a654c), with its record pointer in rsi and the id scalar in edx",
    "after the call the wrapper passes the same scratch to the registrar 0x474f6a0 through slot 0x64e1488 (call site 0x15a6596) and requires a nonzero return",
    "the registrar forwards the pointer unchanged as rdi to the wrap constructor 0x4742470 through slot 0x64eaf70 (call site 0x474f6ad); the constructor passes it on as rsi to the payload constructor 0x4741180, whose head loads the struct words at +0x20/+0x30/+0x38/+0x48 and scales a count by 0x40-byte records",
    "the registrar stores the derived word from its lookup/key helpers into the global cell behind slot 0x64eaf08 (store at 0x474f724), inserts an 8-byte node {wrap pointer} through slot 0x64eaef0, and returns the wrap pointer, or 0 when the insert reports failure",
    "the wrapper stores the returned word at its own out object +0x50 (0x15a65e9) and the record copy at +0x00..+0x50 from its rsi argument; on a zero return it unwrap-fails through slot 0x64df6a0 (call site 0x15a663f)"
  ],
  "verdict": "What consumes the entry tags 0/1/2/3 downstream of the exit reader 0x4749ab0: nothing reads an individual tag value.  The reader itself branches only on the merged entry vector's count (temp+0x60): zero yields the plain 0x50-byte out struct (a verbatim copy of temp[0..0x50]), nonzero yields the {6, ...} form -- discriminant 6 at out+0x00 and the entry vector header {cap, buffer, count} at out+0x08.  The consumer 0x15a3b90, the reader's only caller (slot 0x64e1480, call site 0x15a592a), tests the out word against 6 at 0x15a5930.  On the {6, ...} arm the out union is a Rust Result in its Err variant: the consumer rebuilds the 24-byte entry vector header at [rsp+0xc0] and calls the unwrap-failed helper 0x1680c30 (slot 0x64df6a0) with the message \"called `Result::unwrap()` on an `Err` value\", the error vtable 0x63ffe00 and Location 0x63ffb30 (base/src/log/handle.rs:167:60); the helper formats the Err value through its vtable Debug pointer 0x15b4420 and the panic entry 0x1680e80 aborts, so the arm ends at the ud2 at 0x15a5c77 and the destination is never written.  The vector's storage is released by the vtable drop 0x15ac470, which treats every entry alike: tag <= 3 is only an upper-bound gate before freeing the entry's (+0x10, +0x8) pair, and its sole direct call site in the binary is the consumer's own landing pad at 0x15a6042.  On the plain arm the consumer copies 0x48 bytes (the word at out+0x40, then out[0..0x40]) to the destination pointer held at [rsp+0x278] -- its own rdi argument, saved at 0x15a3ba1.  The consumer's sole direct caller, the wrapper 0x15a6510, supplies a 0x50-byte scratch buffer at its [rsp+0x48] as that destination and, after the return, hands the scratch to the registrar 0x474f6a0 (slot 0x64e1488); the registrar forwards it untouched to the wrap constructor 0x4742470, whose payload constructor 0x4741180 is the first code to read the struct's fields, then registers the result globally and returns the wrap pointer the wrapper stores at its out object +0x50 (a zero return is itself unwrap-failed by the wrapper).  The delegate's per-tag production semantics (0 = vecA duplicate, 1 = third/sub-vector non-member, 2 = vecB duplicate, 3 = vecB colon-scan hit, per the merge-delegate packet) therefore survive downstream only as an aggregate: any leftover entry at all turns the call into an unwrap panic, and no consumer distinguishes 0/1/2/3."
}
